# The build stage installs and compiles from a clean context. Anything a
# developer's checkout happens to have lying around must not reach the image —
# a stale apps/web/dist is the one that would actually get served.
#
# Patterns are matched against the whole path, so `node_modules` alone would
# exclude the root one and copy apps/api/node_modules in beside it. `**/` is
# what makes these mean what they read as.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo

.git
.github
**/.vite
**/.turbo
.mongo-data

# Never. Production configuration arrives as real environment variables from
# the host's secret store; a .env baked into a layer is a published secret.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
